the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the tree diameter is *a number*.
    the protected area is *a truth value*.
    the tree felling permitted is *a text*.
    the protected area or null is *a truth value*.

the templates are:
    the tree felling permitted for *a number* and *a truth value* is *a text* under table tree_felling_permitted.

the table tree_felling_permitted is, with first match:
    tree diameter   | protected area | decision
    <= 30           | any            | "Permit"
    >= 31 and <= 60 | false          | "Permit"
    >= 31 and <= 60 | true           | "Reject"
    > 60            | any            | "Reject"

the knowledge base tree_felling_decision includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/tree-felling-decision.dmn".

the protected area or null is the protected area, as stated in the model at decision Tree Felling Permitted?.

rule tree_felling_permitted_2 with provenance the model at decision Tree Felling Permitted?:
the protected area or null is null if
    it is not the case that the protected area is a truth value.

rule tree_felling_permitted_3 with provenance the model at decision Tree Felling Permitted?:
the tree felling permitted is a text if
    the tree felling permitted for the tree diameter and the protected area or null is the text under table tree_felling_permitted.

